<Page title="How we research products" description="The photographer-first criteria Best Tripod uses to evaluate tripods, monopods, heads and tripod accessories.">
  <p>Every recommendation on {SITE.name} goes through the same photographer-first checklist. We combine manufacturer specifications and user manuals, independent reviews and long-term owner reports, and our own criteria for how a tripod behaves with real gear in real places: a trailhead, a carry-on bin, a windy overlook, a dark sky site.</p>
  <h2>What we check on every tripod</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Real working height.</strong> We separate maximum height with the center column raised from the height with the column down, and we note how close it gets to eye level for an average adult once a camera and head are on top.</li>
    <li><strong>Load capacity against real gear.</strong> We compare the rated load with what people actually mount: a mirrorless body with a 24-70mm, a full-frame camera with a 70-200mm f/2.8, a cinema rig. A rating is a ceiling, not a comfortable working load.</li>
    <li><strong>Folded length and weight.</strong> Will it fit a carry-on, strap to a daypack, or slide into a camera bag? We note folded length with the head attached when the maker lists it.</li>
    <li><strong>Leg locks and build.</strong> Twist or flip locks, number of leg sections, carbon fiber or aluminum, leg angle stops, feet and spikes, and how the head and plate are made.</li>
    <li><strong>Compatibility.</strong> Arca-Swiss plates and clamps, 1/4"-20 and 3/8"-16 threads, bowl or flat bases for video heads, and whether the included head can be swapped.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Keeping guides current</h2>
  <p>Models change and get replaced. We revisit guides regularly, update recommendations when a tripod is discontinued or revised, and show the last-reviewed date on every article. Prices are never hard-coded because they change daily; use the "Check price" buttons for current pricing.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Spotted a wrong spec or an outdated pick? Email us via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and we will review it promptly.</p>
</Page>
